                <pb facs="0605" n="525" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg525"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Leishman to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-07-08"><hi rendition="#italic">July 8,
                        1901</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 56.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring further to my dispatch No. 53 of
                    July 5, I beg to advise that the trouble in regard to the Rev. Mr. Cole at
                    Bitlis has been satisfactorily adjusted, and herewith I inclose copy of
                    correspondence which will explain the matter more fully.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John G. A.
                    Leishman.</hi></signed></closer>




